# RLM-Anchor — System Rules
# This file is auto-read by Cursor AI on EVERY request.
# It contains routing logic for the RLM-Anchor memory system.
# Details → .agent/memory/

# ═══════════════════════════════════════
# 🔴 CRITICAL RULES (always active)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════

# Language: ALWAYS respond in the language from
# .agent/memory/13_preferences/language_local.md (if exists)
# Otherwise: .agent/memory/13_preferences/language.md

# OS: Windows — NEVER use Unix commands (du, wc, find, grep, sed, awk)
# Use PowerShell or built-in agent tools

# ═══════════════════════════════════════
# 🧠 MEMORY-AWARE ROUTING ENGINE
# ═══════════════════════════════════════

# BEFORE generating any response that involves creating,
# editing, or reviewing code/content, you MUST follow this process:

# STEP 1: CLASSIFY the request
#
# | Type         | Trigger keywords                                      |
# |--------------|-------------------------------------------------------|
# | CODE         | write code, create function, add method, refactor     |
# | UI           | page, button, layout, CSS, design, style, template    |
# | ARCHITECTURE | system design, API design, component structure         |
# | DOMAIN       | business logic, business rule, workflow, process       |
# | DEBUG        | bug, error, not working, fix, broken, crash            |
# | DEPLOY       | deploy, server, config, production, CI/CD              |
# | TEST         | test, coverage, QA, edge case                          |
# | GENERAL      | question, explanation, discussion                      |

# STEP 2: READ the required memory files (MANDATORY)
#
# CODE         → .agent/memory/05_code/_index.md → relevant files
#                + .agent/memory/13_preferences/coding_style.md (relevant section)
# UI           → .agent/memory/05_code/conventions.md
#                + coding_style.md (HTML/CSS section) + CUSTOM PROJECT RULES below
# ARCHITECTURE → .agent/memory/02_architecture/_index.md
#                + .agent/memory/03_decisions/_index.md (check existing ADRs)
# DOMAIN       → .agent/memory/04_domain/_index.md → relevant files
# DEBUG        → .agent/memory/06_problems/_index.md → bugs/, workarounds/
# DEPLOY       → .agent/memory/11_deployment/_index.md
# TEST         → .agent/memory/10_testing/_index.md
# GENERAL      → No memory reading required
#
# KEY: Read _index.md first → it tells you which files exist.
# Read ONLY the files relevant to the current request.

# STEP 3: APPLY rules from memory + CUSTOM RULES below

# STEP 4: SELF-CHECK (for CODE/UI)
# Before finalizing output, verify:
# - Follows conventions from 05_code/conventions.md?
# - Follows coding_style.md rules?
# - Avoids patterns from 06_problems/?
# - Complies with CUSTOM PROJECT RULES?

# ═══════════════════════════════════════
# 🟢 MEMORY SYSTEM
# ═══════════════════════════════════════

# This project uses RLM-Anchor persistent memory.
# Memory: .agent/memory/ (13 categories)
# Index: .agent/MEMORY_INDEX.md
# Commands: /wakeup, /sleep, /remember, /recall, /anchor_sync

# ═══════════════════════════════════════
# 🎯 CUSTOM PROJECT RULES
# ═══════════════════════════════════════

# ADD YOUR PROJECT-SPECIFIC RULES BELOW THIS LINE.
# These are checked on EVERY request that involves CODE or UI.
# Keep rules short and specific.
#
# Example rules (replace with your own):
#   - NEVER use white or light backgrounds for buttons
#   - ALWAYS use CSS variables: var(--btn-primary), var(--bg-main)
#   - ALWAYS use dark theme colors from project palette
#   - Django templates: spaces around == in {% if %}, tags on single line
#   - API responses must include error codes and messages

# ═══════════════════════════════════════
# 📖 MEMORY CATEGORIES REFERENCE
# ═══════════════════════════════════════
# 01_project     → Project overview, tech stack
# 02_architecture → System design
# 03_decisions   → ADRs (check before architectural choices)
# 04_domain      → Business logic
# 05_code        → Code conventions, models, APIs
# 06_problems    → Known bugs, workarounds (check before fixing)
# 07_context     → Session history, pending tasks
# 08_people      → Team roles
# 09_external    → External APIs, integrations
# 10_testing     → Test strategies
# 11_deployment  → Deploy configs
# 12_roadmap     → Future plans, tech debt
# 13_preferences → Code style, language, communication
